    {
      "id": "case-templates-apply-missing-template",
      "behaviors": [
        "bhv-templates-apply-scaffolds-options"
      ],
      "context": [],
      "scenarioContext": {
        "sdim-operation": "templates-apply",
        "sdim-config-source": "image",
        "sdim-container-state": "none",
        "sdim-features": "none",
        "sdim-layering": "single",
        "sdim-output-mode": "human"
      },
      "inputClass": "malformed",
      "oracleType": "spec-expectation",
      "resourceGroup": "fs-heavy",
      "operations": [
        {
          "id": "op-apply",
          "subcommand": "templates-apply",
          "argv": [
            "${WORKSPACE}/broken",
            "--output",
            "${WORKSPACE}/applied"
          ],
          "fixtures": [
            "fx-templates-minimal"
          ],
          "expectFailurePhase": "exec"
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "channel": "chan-exit-code",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "nonZero": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "cleanup": {
        "tempdir": true
      },
      "notes": "FR-040 malformed class: the named directory exists but carries no `devcontainer-template.json`, so it is not a template. The directory is chosen deliberately over a NON-EXISTENT path: a path that resolves to nothing locally falls through to an OCI registry lookup, and the case would then be measuring the network rather than the parse."
    },
    {
      "id": "case-templates-apply-multifile-tree",
      "behaviors": [
        "bhv-templates-apply-scaffolds-options"
      ],
      "context": [],
      "scenarioContext": {
        "sdim-operation": "templates-apply",
        "sdim-config-source": "dockerfile",
        "sdim-container-state": "none",
        "sdim-features": "none",
        "sdim-layering": "cli-overlay",
        "sdim-output-mode": "human"
      },
      "inputClass": "valid",
      "oracleType": "spec-expectation",
      "resourceGroup": "fs-heavy",
      "operations": [
        {
          "id": "op-apply",
          "subcommand": "templates-apply",
          "argv": [
            "${WORKSPACE}/template",
            "--output",
            "${WORKSPACE}/applied",
            "--option",
            "imageVariant=3.20"
          ],
          "fixtures": [
            "fx-templates-multifile"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "channel": "chan-exit-code",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "equals": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-filesystem",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "exists": "applied/scripts/post-create.sh"
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-filesystem",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "absent": "applied/devcontainer-template.json"
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-filesystem",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "mode": {
              "applied/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json": "0644"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-file-content",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "jsonSubset": {
              "applied/.devcontainer/Dockerfile": "FROM alpine:3.20\n"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "fsAllowlist": [
        "applied/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json",
        "applied/.devcontainer/Dockerfile",
        "applied/scripts/post-create.sh",
        "applied/devcontainer-template.json"
      ],
      "cleanup": {
        "tempdir": true
      },
      "notes": "The third covering case for `chan-filesystem` (SC-005's floor), and the one that asserts scaffolding as a TREE rather than as a single document. Three separate claims, each its own predicate. `exists`: a file outside `.devcontainer/` is scaffolded too — a template is a directory, not a configuration file. `absent`: `devcontainer-template.json` is template METADATA and must not land in the user's project; a naive whole-tree copy leaves it behind and every other assertion still passes. `mode`: the scaffolded configuration's permissions are observed, not just its bytes. The `chan-file-content` assertion pins the option substituted into the DOCKERFILE, not the configuration — substitution that only walks `devcontainer.json` produces a scaffolded tree with a raw `${templateOption:...}` in it. Also closes the `dockerfile` x `cli-overlay` pair. NOT asserted, deliberately: the template's script is committed executable and is scaffolded `0644`, so deacon drops the executable bit. That is a real observation with no reference side (the pinned reference cannot apply a LOCAL template directory at all, so there is nothing to differentiate against); pinning either mode here would record an unreviewed judgement as an expectation."
    },
    {
      "id": "case-templates-apply-option-substituted",
      "behaviors": [
        "bhv-templates-apply-scaffolds-options"
      ],
      "context": [],
      "scenarioContext": {
        "sdim-operation": "templates-apply",
        "sdim-config-source": "image",
        "sdim-container-state": "none",
        "sdim-features": "none",
        "sdim-layering": "cli-overlay",
        "sdim-output-mode": "human"
      },
      "inputClass": "valid",
      "oracleType": "spec-expectation",
      "resourceGroup": "fs-heavy",
      "operations": [
        {
          "id": "op-apply",
          "subcommand": "templates-apply",
          "argv": [
            "${WORKSPACE}/template",
            "--output",
            "${WORKSPACE}/applied",
            "--option",
            "imageVariant=3.20"
          ],
          "fixtures": [
            "fx-templates-minimal"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "channel": "chan-exit-code",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "equals": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-filesystem",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "exists": "applied/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json"
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-file-content",
          "operation": "op-apply",
          "assertion": {
            "jsonSubset": {
              "applied/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json": "{\n\t\"name\": \"conformance-minimal\",\n\t\"image\": \"alpine:3.20\"\n}\n"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "fsAllowlist": [
        "applied/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json"
      ],
      "cleanup": {
        "tempdir": true
      },
      "notes": "Covers the high-risk triple `hrt-templates-apply-cli-overlay-image-human`, and FR-005 for the operation. The template's option is supplied on the command line and the ONLY evidence it arrived is the scaffolded bytes: the operation emits no result document. An option that is parsed but never substituted produces a successful run and a configuration containing the raw placeholder, so the file-content assertion is the whole case. Runs `fs-heavy` in an isolated temp workspace — it WRITES, and the committed fixture tree is shared input."
    },
    {
      "id": "case-templates-apply-unsupported-option",
      "behaviors": [
        "bhv-templates-apply-scaffolds-options"
      ],
      "context": [],
      "scenarioContext": {
        "sdim-operation": "templates-apply",
        "sdim-config-source": "image",
        "sdim-container-state": "none",
        "sdim-features": "none",
        "sdim-layering": "cli-overlay",
        "sdim-output-mode": "human"
      },
      "inputClass": "unsupported",
      "oracleType": "spec-expectation",
      "resourceGroup": "fs-heavy",
      "operations": [
        {
          "id": "op-apply",
          "subcommand": "templates-apply",
          "argv": [
            "${WORKSPACE}/template",
